d 'SVYLET': module to perform Wald omnibus F-test, Bonferroni, and Compact Letter Display for means/proportions/totals under svy
d
d  svylet tests whether a mean, proportion, or total differs across
d the categories of an over() variable (e.g., survey year) under a
d complex survey design, and reports the result as a Compact Letter
d Display (CLD) -- the familiar Tukey/Duncan-style letter grouping
d from agronomic ANOVA post-hoc tables (categories sharing a letter
d are not significantly different), adapted here to a design-based
d Wald test rather than classical ANOVA. It reports a design-based
d Wald omnibus F-test (with the Korn & Graubard 1990 small-sample
d adjustment, matching Stata's own default for test/testparm after
d svy:), all pairwise comparisons with Bonferroni correction, and
d the resulting letter groups. All three stat() modes share one
d Mata engine that operates directly on e(b)/e(V)/e(df_r), so the
d same code works after svy: mean, svy: proportion, and svy: total
d without depending on margins/testparm chaining correctly after
d non-regress estimation commands. An optional boot() setting
d recalibrates the omnibus F-test by prepivoting (Beran 1988),
d using a bootstrap that resamples the pooled observations across
d over() categories (Rao, Wu & Yue 1992; Beaumont & Patak 2012) and
d reassigns group labels at random to enforce the null hypothesis
d in the resampling itself (Hall & Wilson 1991). 
d
d KW: Wald
d KW: Bonferroni
d KW: means
d KW: proportions
d KW: totals
d KW: complex survey data
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260828
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f svylet.ado
f svylet.sthlp
f svylet_es.sthlp
